 "greekNote": "Greek block starts at y=60; look extra chars up by 'glyphs' (the index formula in howToFind is for ASCII only). Default advance is 6 px. Lowercase accents (άέήίόύώ) use a 2px tonos in rows 0-1 on the right. Accented capitals (ΆΈΉΊΌΎΏ) live on row y=110 in 8px cells: 2px tonos in column 0 rows 0-1, a 1px gap, then the unchanged 5px capital in columns 2-6 (w 7, advance 8). ΪΫ: dialytika on row 0, row 1 blank, letter compressed to rows 2-6. ΐ: tonos row 0, dialytika row 1. ΰ: dialytika and tonos on row 0. All-caps copy uses unaccented capitals. U+037E maps to ';', U+0387 to U+00B7. Guillemets «» sit on the extra row at (42,100) and (48,100)."
